{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he lay with her and afflicted her</b> — \"and he lay with her\" is in the usual manner; \"and he afflicted her\" is not in the usual manner (Genesis Rabbah 80:5) — this is the language of Rashi. But Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 34:2) that \"and he afflicted her\" means because she was a virgin. There is no need for this, for any act of intercourse in which he forces her is called עִנּוּי. Thus: \"you shall not have dominion over her, because you have afflicted her\" (Deuteronomy 21:14), and likewise: \"and they afflicted my concubine and she died\" (Judges 20:5). And Scripture tells us that she was forced and did not consent to the prince of the land, to recount her praise."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:24.892737657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}